# Cook one piece of raw meat in a furnace within four blocks (`smelt` takes the
# cooked item and needs fuel, which it checks itself). A core skill of its own,
# not part of `get_food`: raw meat already counts as food, and a furnace is a
# later rung than the first night (decision 2026-11-09 "Five next areas").
#
# Why the rules are ordered this way: nothing happens without a furnace in
# reach, so every action rule carries the `near(furnace, 4)` guard; beef first
# (the most common), then pork, mutton and chicken. A `smelt` that fails
# (`no_fuel`, `needs_furnace`) makes its rule ineligible for one tick and the
# next rule gets a turn; the last rule ends the skill, so it never loops.
skill cook_food()
  doc "Cook one raw meat (beef, porkchop, mutton or chicken) in a furnace within 4 blocks."
  rules:
    near(furnace, 4) and count(beef) >= 1 -> smelt(cooked_beef)
    near(furnace, 4) and count(porkchop) >= 1 -> smelt(cooked_porkchop)
    near(furnace, 4) and count(mutton) >= 1 -> smelt(cooked_mutton)
    near(furnace, 4) and count(chicken) >= 1 -> smelt(cooked_chicken)
    true -> done
